attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 15, `ulaF` to `yjfK`, are carried by 91 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 8% of calls {S1}. The model names 93 to 99% of them, fewest at column 15, `yjfK`, 93% {S1}.

@variable **A short variable stretch follows**, columns 16 to 17, `yjfJ` and `yjfI`, carried by 87 to 88% {S2}. The `ula` genes, columns 0 to 7, are [[ascorbate transport and catabolism]] {S1, Q}. At the end a branch runs through columns 62 to 79, [[lysine decarboxylation]], carried by 29 to 64%, the stretch most in regions of plasticity, 31 to 88% {S8, P, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 97 against 79%, and hesitates less there, 0.19 against 0.95 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 64, `cadA`, a variable column, 1.57 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork and variable columns.** Columns 62 to 79 are carried by 29 to 64% of chromosomes, 13 persistent and 5 shell {S8}. The last column is `adiA`, in 29% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 92% of genes**, 0.40 bits on average, perplexity 1.6 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 2.03 against 0.15 bits, and names fewer genes, 60% against 97% {C}.

